    "reason": "[ev-3c176b54b173] and [ev-e77b6a01ac75] say that `applications, update` and `applications, delete` used to implicitly grant update/delete on an application's sub-resources. Now they cover only the Application itself, and `update/*` and `delete/*` are needed for sub-resources. That is the same configuration with different meaning, so behavior-changed fits. [ev-a56a8cf82a6c] and [ev-f1b8b1838187] call it disabling fine-grained inheritance by default. The changed files in [ev-69d0a032cb9a] (util/settings/settings.go) suggest a controlling setting, but no excerpt names its key or before/after values, so a config-key or default-changed subject can't be built and the free-form protocol-behavior name rbac-fine-grained-inheritance is a reasonable fallback.",
